-- 2) Retire 466 (invented MSU award name)
UPDATE scholarships SET title = 'Lomonosov Moscow State University "International Excellence Scholarship" (retired — no such award; funded study runs through the Russian Government Quota and olympiad quota routes)', coverage_type = 'Unspecified', amount_usd_value = 0, deadline = 'No such award exists — do not apply. Tuition-free study at MSU is reached through the Russian Government Quota selection in the home country and olympiad quota routes, not through an MSU scholarship application', degree_levels = '["Bachelor''s","Master''s","PhD"]', eligible_majors = '["All Majors"]', min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL, merit_based = true, description = 'This record is retired because Lomonosov Moscow State University publishes no "International Excellence Scholarship". The university''s English admissions pages, read for this record on 2026-10-28, describe a single admission system for foreign citizens: competitive entrance examinations (Russian language and a specialisation subject at bachelor and specialist level, separate examinations per master''s programme), enrolment by examination points, and — for the fee-paying route — an educational contract signed with the faculty. Most programmes are taught in Russian, with a preparatory course at the Institute of Russian Language and Culture recommended. Tuition-free ("budget") study exists in the Russian system, but it is not an MSU award an applicant can apply for: quota places are allocated by the Government of the Russian Federation through selection in the applicant''s home country (Rossotrudnichestvo) — catalogued separately in this database as the Russian Government Quota (Rossotrudnichestvo) — or won through olympiad quota routes such as the Open Doors: Russian Scholarship Project, also catalogued separately; narrow categories of foreign citizens may additionally enter on equal terms with Russian citizens under interstate agreements. None of these channels is an institutional excellence scholarship run by MSU, and the university publishes no award of that name, value or application procedure. The imported name is therefore withdrawn rather than rewritten, and the real routes are the separate catalogue records named above.', requirements = 'Do not apply for an MSU "International Excellence Scholarship" — none exists. For funded study at MSU: (1) the Russian Government Quota — selection is run in the home country through Rossotrudnichestvo; see the separate catalogue record for its procedure and cycle; (2) olympiad quota routes such as Open Doors for master''s and doctoral study, also catalogued separately; (3) otherwise MSU admission is a fee-paying contract route: choose a programme (most are taught in Russian; a pre-university preparatory course exists), contact the faculty international admissions office for tuition, examination dates and visa rules, prepare legalised education documents with notarised Russian translations plus an education-recognition application, apply via the MSU online platform, and pass the competitive entrance examinations.', website_url = 'https://www.msu.ru/en/admissions/', eligible_countries = '["All"]', funding_type = 'Retired: imported name; MSU publishes no such scholarship (funded routes are the government quota and olympiad quotas)', tuition_coverage = 'No MSU-funded international scholarship exists to describe. MSU''s own application process for the fee-paying route ends with signing an educational contract with the faculty. Tuition-free budget places reach foreign citizens only through the Russian Government Quota selection in the home country, olympiad quota wins, or equal-terms categories under interstate agreements — each catalogued or governed outside this record.', living_allowance = NULL, travel_allowance = NULL, accommodation = NULL, application_fee = NULL, english_requirements = 'Not applicable: most MSU programmes are taught in Russian (entrance examinations include Russian language at bachelor and specialist level, with a preparatory Russian course recommended); a smaller list of programmes is taught in English. The university pages publish no IELTS score for a scholarship, because there is no such scholarship.', required_documents = '[]', application_url = 'https://www.msu.ru/en/admissions/', opening_date = NULL, deadline_date = NULL, deadline_type = 'not_published', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL, rounds = '[]', recurrence = 'annual', expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, application_status = 'closed', last_verified_at = '2026-10-28 19:30:00+05', last_updated_at = '2026-10-28 19:30:00+05', verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 9, source_url = 'https://www.msu.ru/en/admissions/', notes = 'RETIRED in Pass 125 on 2026-10-28 as an invented (imported) award name. Provenance: the 2026-10-26 decontamination had already stripped an invented USD 6,000 and deadline from this row and left it at reliability 4 because the university page could not be read then. On 2026-10-28 two official MSU pages were read in full: the admissions index (source 1131, pre-existing) and the application process for international students (source 3145). Together they describe competitive entrance-examination admission (Russian language + specialisation; per-programme master''s examinations), enrolment by points, a fee-paying educational contract, legalisation/translation/recognition of foreign education documents, and links to equal-terms admission categories — and no university scholarship of any name, let alone an International Excellence Scholarship. Honest limitation: the English pages display 2024-cycle dates; they are the university''s current admissions pages and the negative finding does not depend on cycle. Real funded routes already in this catalogue: Russian Government Quota (Rossotrudnichestvo) at reliability 9 and Open Doors: Russian Scholarship Project at reliability 10, alongside university olympiad records; several duplicate quota rows were retired in earlier Russia-cluster passes. The university_scholarships row carrying the invented name at Lomonosov Moscow State University (university 84, row 489) was deleted with this retirement. Retain inactive; do not revive under this name.', is_active = false, university_id = 84, award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = NULL, award_basis = NULL WHERE id = 466;

-- 3) Retire 503 (invented UCT award name)
UPDATE scholarships SET title = 'University of Cape Town "International Excellence Scholarship" (retired — no such award; UCT''s real international scholarships are supplementary and the 2026 call did not open)', coverage_type = 'Unspecified', amount_usd_value = 0, deadline = 'No such award exists — do not apply. UCT''s real scheme for international postgraduates (supplementary contributions, not full cost) did not open its 2026 call, and no 2027 call had been published at verification on 2026-10-28', degree_levels = '["Master''s","PhD"]', eligible_majors = '["All Majors"]', min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL, merit_based = true, description = 'This record is retired because the University of Cape Town runs no "International Excellence Scholarship". UCT''s genuine provision for international students is its international and refugee scholarships for postgraduate study in any discipline — a limited number awarded competitively each year, with preference to senior candidates. The university states on its own page, read for this record on 2026-10-28: "All UCT international and refugee students'' scholarships are supplementary as a contribution towards the cost of attendance. Students who apply must have the means to fund their studies." A notice on the same page adds: "The call for applications for 2026 will not open, due to funding constraints." No 2027 call had been published when the page was read. The scheme is therefore neither an excellence flagship nor currently open: it is a suspended, supplementary top-up whose previously published values were R25,000 for an honours year, R30,000 for a master''s and R35,000 for a doctorate (per the UCT financial assistance handbook, as recorded on this catalogue''s dedicated record for the UCT scheme). The applicant''s country of origin has no bearing on the award, so a student from Uzbekistan would be eligible to compete if a call reopens — but it would never make the degree fully funded, and an applicant must first apply for full-time admission. Everything else in the UCT funding landscape is narrower: the university''s merit and need awards are restricted to South African citizens and permanent residents, and the Mastercard Foundation Scholars Program at UCT is limited to sub-Saharan Africa. The imported "excellence" name is withdrawn rather than rewritten; the real scheme is documented on the dedicated UCT record in this catalogue, which remains inactive while the call is suspended.', requirements = 'Do not apply for a UCT "International Excellence Scholarship" — none exists. The real UCT international and refugee scholarships are postgraduate, supplementary contributions (not full cost: "Students who apply must have the means to fund their studies"), competitive with preference to senior candidates, and require a full-time admission application to UCT first. The 2026 call did not open because of funding constraints and no 2027 call was published at verification on 2026-10-28; the postgraduate funding office also cannot extend funding beyond tenure (third-year master''s and fourth-year doctoral registrations and above). Treat UCT as a self-funded option unless a new call appears on the university''s international and refugee scholarships page; country of origin has no bearing on that award, but UCT merit and need awards are limited to South African citizens and permanent residents.', website_url = 'https://uct.ac.za/students/fees-funding-postgraduate-degree-funding-bursaries-scholarships/international-and-refugee-scholarships', eligible_countries = '["All"]', funding_type = 'Retired: imported name; UCT publishes no such scholarship (its real international scheme is supplementary and currently suspended)', tuition_coverage = 'No UCT excellence award exists to describe. UCT''s real international and refugee scholarships are, in the university''s words, "supplementary as a contribution towards the cost of attendance", and students who apply "must have the means to fund their studies". Previously published values (financial assistance handbook, recorded on the dedicated catalogue record): R25,000 honours, R30,000 master''s, R35,000 doctorate, renewable on satisfactory progress. The 2026 call did not open due to funding constraints.', living_allowance = NULL, travel_allowance = NULL, accommodation = NULL, application_fee = NULL, english_requirements = 'Not applicable to a nonexistent award; the English requirement of the admitted UCT programme would apply to any future call of the real scheme.', required_documents = '[]', application_url = 'https://uct.ac.za/students/fees-funding-postgraduate-degree-funding-bursaries-scholarships/international-and-refugee-scholarships', opening_date = NULL, deadline_date = NULL, deadline_type = 'not_published', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL, rounds = '[]', recurrence = 'annual', expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, application_status = 'closed', last_verified_at = '2026-10-28 19:30:00+05', last_updated_at = '2026-10-28 19:30:00+05', verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 9, source_url = 'https://uct.ac.za/students/fees-funding-postgraduate-degree-funding-bursaries-scholarships/international-and-refugee-scholarships', notes = 'RETIRED in Pass 125 on 2026-10-28 as an invented (imported) award name. Provenance: the 2026-10-26 decontamination had already stripped an invented USD 6,500 and deadline from this row and left it at reliability 4 because UCT pages then returned HTTP 500; its stored URL (uct.ac.za/apply) now returns 404. On 2026-10-28 UCT''s own international and refugee scholarships page (source 3146) was read directly: it describes the real scheme (postgraduate, competitive, preference to senior candidates, full-time admission application first, country of origin has no bearing), states verbatim that all such scholarships are "supplementary as a contribution towards the cost of attendance" and that students "must have the means to fund their studies", and carries the notice "The call for applications for 2026 will not open, due to funding constraints" with no 2027 call published. Handbook 14 values (R25,000/R30,000/R35,000) and the 30 August preceding-year deadline are recorded on the dedicated catalogue record 704 ("UCT Financial Aid for International Students (retired, call suspended)"), retired earlier for exactly this suspension; Pass 125 re-read the page first-hand and raised that record''s provenance accordingly. UCT merit/need awards are for South African citizens and permanent residents; the Mastercard Foundation Scholars Program at UCT is limited to sub-Saharan Africa — so no open UCT scholarship exists for a student from Uzbekistan at verification. Degree levels narrowed to master''s/PhD to match the real scheme the name mimicked. The university_scholarships row carrying the invented name at the University of Cape Town (university 192, row 664) was deleted with this retirement. Retain inactive; do not revive under this name. If UCT publishes a new call, revisit record 704 (the real scheme), not this row.', is_active = false, university_id = 192, award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = NULL, award_basis = NULL WHERE id = 503;

-- 4) 704 provenance upgrade (append is not idempotent; replay once)
UPDATE scholarships SET source_reliability = 9, last_verified_at = '2026-10-28 19:30:00+05', last_updated_at = '2026-10-28 19:30:00+05', notes = notes || ' PASS 125 FIRST-HAND RECHECK 2026-10-28: the UCT page that returned HTTP 500 on 2026-10-25 has now been read directly (source 3146), and it confirms the load-bearing statements verbatim — "All UCT international and refugee students'' scholarships are supplementary as a contribution towards the cost of attendance. Students who apply must have the means to fund their studies." and the notice "The call for applications for 2026 will not open, due to funding constraints." The page adds that awards are competitive with preference to senior candidates, that applicants must apply for full-time admission first, that country of origin has no bearing, that full details sit in Handbook 14, and that the postgraduate funding office cannot extend funding beyond tenure (third-year master''s and fourth-year doctoral registrations and above). No 2027 call had been published at this recheck. The retirement therefore stands on directly read evidence and source_reliability rises from 4 to 9; the imported duplicate name "International Excellence Scholarship" (record 503) was retired in the same pass. The row remains inactive — revisit only if UCT publishes a new call.' WHERE id = 704;

